{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs1chpTJG7taEJiWRtcB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in place. Issue #1146 is resolved: `get_metadata_for_wheel()` now reads the wheel's own `{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA` instead of the first `.dist-info/METADATA` it finds. Tests pass (77 passed, 2 skipped, up from 65 passed, 2 skipped), and ruff check and format are clean. mypy could not run because its module is missing from the environment, and I did not run the full test suite.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/pkgmetadata/pep376.py`** (new): `verbatim_dist_name()` and `dist_info_name()`. Both validate with `parse_wheel_filename` first, so bad names and non-wheel extensions raise `InvalidWheelFilename`. Both are exported from `fromager.pkgmetadata`.\n- **`src/fromager/candidate.py`**: `_wheel_metadata_path(url)` takes the last path segment, ignores the query and fragment, and returns `f\"{dist_info_name(filename)}/METADATA\"`. The fallback reads exactly that member and raises `ValueError` if it is missing.\n- **`src/fromager/wheels.py`** and **`src/fromager/dependencies.py`**: both replace their `split(\"-\", 1)[0]` logic with the new helpers. In `dependencies.py` I used `dist_info_name` for the METADATA path, which is a slight behavior change: the version now comes verbatim from the filename rather than from `Version`, so it matches the `.dist-info` name exactly.\n- **Tests**: `tests/test_pep376.py` covers the helpers, including the invalid-filename cases. `tests/test_candidate.py` (new) covers the path helper and the fallback. The fallback test builds a real in-memory wheel with a vendored `.dist-info` listed first, which is the bug from the issue. It fails on the old code.\n\n**Decisions to check**\n\n- **Two existing tests changed.** `test_get_metadata_pep658_fallback_behavior` and `test_get_metadata_without_pep658_behavior` used the wheel URL `test-package-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl`. A dash in the distribution name is invalid, so the new validation rejected it. Those tests only passed before because they swallowed every exception. I changed only the wheel filename in those two to `test_package-...`. Their assertions are untouched. Say if you would rather keep the dashed name and relax the validation instead.\n- **Percent-decoding.** `_wheel_metadata_path` unquotes the filename, so `%2B` in local versions resolves to `+`. This wasn't in the spec, but without it those URLs would fail validation.\n\nI did not commit anything, since you didn't ask for a commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5652,"cache_read_input_tokens":116278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5652},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb586e58-4115-4292-b161-9d13f431fb36","uuid":"b5275166-da72-49bf-a5dc-ecaa9e84fb17","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:53:17.976Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs1chPR6ZuGXzAToA3bY"}
